# =============================================================================
# What reaches the remote: docs/ and this file. That is all.
#
# docs/ IS THE WEBSITE. Not documentation. GitHub Pages has a built-in option
# to serve a repo's /docs folder, which is why it has that name. Everything
# inside it is the finished, static site: HTML, CSS, JS, images.
#
# NOTE: free GitHub Pages requires a PUBLIC repository. Anything committed is
# readable by anyone who finds it, so treat this file as the boundary between
# what is published and what stays on the build machine. Nothing internal
# belongs on the far side of it, including in these comments.
# =============================================================================

# --- secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
*.key
*.pem

# --- markdown ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Notes, specs and handover documents all stay local.
*.md

# --- the generator ----------------------------------------------------------
# tools/ builds docs/. The remote only needs the built output, so the generator
# stays on this machine. Consequence: a fresh clone can serve the site but
# cannot rebuild it. Keep this folder backed up somewhere.
tools/

# --- source material, not site assets ---------------------------------------
# Originals only. Everything the site actually serves is built into
# docs/assets/img/ by tools/build_images.py.
Information img/
documentation/
candidates/
models-in/
*.docx

# --- archive ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Things that were in docs/ and are no longer part of the site. Kept because
# they are useful again later, ignored because they are not the site. The
# photograph picker lives here once the client has chosen.
archive/

# --- build scratch ----------------------------------------------------------
# Downloads, intermediate models, contact sheets. All reproducible.
.work/

# --- superseded -------------------------------------------------------------
mrs-aircraft-site/

# --- local tooling ----------------------------------------------------------
.agents/
.claude/
skills-lock.json

# --- os and editor ----------------------------------------------------------
~$*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
